<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Traidenis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1282">1282</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Traidenis was grand duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> from about 1269 to 1282, a pagan ruler who restored the power of the state after the turmoil following the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindaugas">Mindaugas</a>. He fought the Livonian Order and the princes of Galicia-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volhynia">Volhynia</a>, and supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semigallians">Semigallians</a> and Prussians against the crusading orders. His reign prepared the way for the rise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vytenis">Vytenis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gediminas">Gediminas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/traidenis.jpg" alt="Traidenis" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexander Guagnini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lithuanian_Grand_Duke_Traidenis.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
